      "writtenOn": "2023-09-26T23:17:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is broken, but not for the reason you describe.\n\nExcluding @bazel_tools from the query itself doesn\u0027t mean that all rdeps of @bazel_tools are unqueryable. That would make query syntax incredibly broken.\n\n(In fact, for any `A -\u003e B`,the query `deps(A) except B` would necessarily fail. That\u0027d be pretty useless...)\n\nThe reason is that `@bazel_tools//...` seems unqueryable, so bazel can\u0027t actually expand that string in a meaningful fashion.\n\n\nSince this is a bit nontrivial to solve this way, I\u0027ll approve this CL and we can continue as-is.",
      "parentUuid": "588590dc_8c7a6497",
      "revId": "26beeef3c8669856fe5cd6575cf4c9cdcdcba0f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
