      "writtenOn": "2023-09-27T15:09:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure what you meant by \"necessarily fail\", i.e. I tried the following:\n```\n$ tree\n.\n├── BUILD\n└── WORKSPACE\n$ cat BUILD\nfilegroup(name \u003d \"B\")\nfilegroup(name \u003d \"A\", data \u003d [\":B\"])\nusta4:~/scratch$ bazel query \"deps(A)\"\n//:A\n//:B\nusta4:~/scratch$ bazel query \"deps(A) except B\"\n//:A\n```\nI do see that query involving \"@bazel_tools/...\" fails by reporting `Error: file \u0027@rules_proto//proto:defs.bzl\u0027 does not contain symbol \u0027proto_lang_toolchain\u0027`\nI can get past that with `--keep-going` but that would ignore all missing targets indiscriminately and hinder early discovery of bugs.\n\nNote ` bazel query \"deps(@bazel_tools//tools/cpp:current_cc_toolchain)\"` works fine for instance. Maybe `rules_proto` needs to be updated.",
      "parentUuid": "23f1ebe3_f54b3606",
      "revId": "26beeef3c8669856fe5cd6575cf4c9cdcdcba0f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "23640623_b8ab794c",
        "filename": "bazel/aquery.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 382,
      "author": {
        "id": 1605027
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-27T15:21:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My point is that the problem is that `@bazel_tools//...` does not analyze correctly. \n\nYou stated:\n\n\u003e but if we exclude @bazel_tools from the query itself then it will fail because they are dependencies of other targets.\n\nThis fails, but not for the reason you imply: It is fine to, in the general case, exclude targets from a query that other targets depend on. The problem here is `@bazel_tools//...` is not resolvable.\n\nIf you were to attempt your scratch above (`bazel query \"deps(A) except B\"`) in a non-Android repository, such as a fresh Bazel checkout, it should succeed.\n\nDoes that explain things?",
      "parentUuid": "2bdcdf77_1b53693e",
      "revId": "26beeef3c8669856fe5cd6575cf4c9cdcdcba0f3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
